pigeoncam (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging. Nothing is enabled or started on install -
    run pigeoncam-setup.sh then pigeoncam-doctor.sh (see
    /usr/share/doc/pigeoncam/README.Debian). See
    docs/development/design/debian-packaging.md for the packaging
    decisions this build embodies, in particular the yt-dlp
    Recommends-not-Depends choice and why config.yaml is generated by
    postinst rather than shipped as a conffile.
  * postinst attempts the YouTube API integration's Python virtualenv
    automatically, on every install and upgrade - reaching the network to
    do so, best-effort and never fatal to the install. This package does
    not target the official Debian archive, so the usual "postinst must
    work offline" caution does not bind it.

 -- Jean-Marc Liotier <jm@liotier.org>  Mon, 24 Aug 2026 09:42:52 +0000
